  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1140 AM CDT Wed Jun 10 2026\n\nA cold front is forecast to approach the area on Friday, though\nwill slowly become detached from the parent upper-level wave \nthroughout the day. Regardless, this will be the primary focus for\ndevelopment of showers and thunderstorms, particularly in the \nafternoon as diurnal heating occurs. Activity could become quite \nwidespread by late afternoon, especially across the Plateau. Some \nstorms could be strong to even severe mainly posing a threat for \ndamaging wind gusts. After the front moves through Friday night \nwe'll get a break from the weather on Saturday with more stable \nconditions. However, moisture and instability return to the area \non Sunday which will support continued chances for showers and \nstorms into early next week.",
